ames":18,"team_news":true},"h2h":[],"analyst_view":{"overall":"Brighton (5th of 36, 7 points) host Universitatea Craiova (8th, also 7 points), so a top-eight place is at stake for both. Brighton lost 2-0 at Hull on Sunday and play Newcastle at the weekend, and the match-day team-news page expects rotation: Struijk and Gomez are listed as rested, Azeez (abdominal strain), Yalcouye and Boscagli (Hurzeler said he is struggling with illness) as out, and Hadjam, Minteh and Chema Andres as doubts, none of which the numbers list. Mitoma, Ferguson, Tzimas and Yohanna are out and already counted. Craiova, top in Romania, report no new absences and have named a settled eleven; keeper Isenko's absence is counted. German referee Matthias Jollenbeck (5.3 cards a game in three on record) is already counted, so I keep only a small cut on Brighton's attack for rotation, a touch bigger than this morning.","goals":{"lean":"lower","adjust_pct":-4,"call":"Around 3.4 goals","text":"The numbers say 3.5 goals, 2.9 of them for Brighton, and already take Mitoma, Ferguson and Tzimas into account. A rotated Brighton side with Newcastle next, Minteh doubtful and Azeez out, against a settled, compact Craiova side, points slightly lower, so I go to about 3.4."},"corners":{"lean":"same","adjust_pct":0,"call":"Around 10 to 11 corners","text":"The numbers say 10.6 corners, 8.2 of them for Brighton, who should have long spells of possession against a Craiova side that defends deep with wing-backs dropping into a back five. That pattern drives corners whichever Brighton players start, so I stay at 10.6."},"cards":{"lean":"same","adjust_pct":0,"call":"Around 4 cards","text":"The numbers say 4.2 cards and already add about 6% for referee Matthias Jöllenbeck, who has shown 5.3 cards a game in his three on record. Craiova will spend long periods defending and pick up the larger share (2.6), which the numbers expect; with no rivalry and no change of officials, I stay at 4.2."},"shots":{"lean":"lower","adj